Every check this browser can make holds

holds · record-hash — the record's canonical bytes hash to the hash it is delivered with
holds · prev-link — the record follows from the one before it
holds · inclusion-path — the path leads from the record's hash to the root
holds · root — the root is the root of the record's own cycle
holds · published — the root and its token stand in the published list, and the list runs unbroken
not checked here · tsa-token — the token's signature is not checked in a browser; python -m record verify checks it with OpenSSL
holds · beacon-round — the round is of drand quicknet, and its randomness is the hash of its signature
not checked here · beacon-signature — the round's BLS signature is not checked in a browser; the command line checks it
holds · order — the order is the one the round gives, the pages read follow it, the first pick heads them, and the page is among the picks
not checked here · committed — the commitment token's signature is not checked in a browser; the command line checks it
holds · before-beacon — the candidates were dated before the round, and the round is the first one after: the round chose, not the Bureau
requests beyond the file itself: []
